WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.009
Nothing breaks a training video like a narrator who says your company name wrong.

2
00:00:06.059 --> 00:00:07.124
The good news?

3
00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:09.900
The fix almost always lives in your script.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.344
A voice reads exactly what's written and guesses at the rest.

5
00:00:14.394 --> 00:00:19.036
So listen to the whole narration first, and note every word that sounds off.

6
00:00:19.536 --> 00:00:24.408
If the voice reads WHS as a word, add spaces between the letters.

7
00:00:24.458 --> 00:00:29.077
For names, write them how they sound, and keep the real spelling on the slide.

8
00:00:29.577 --> 00:00:33.718
Voices read numbers literally, so write them as people say them.

9
00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:38.665
Spell out symbols and units, and rephrase any word with two pronunciations.

10
00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:44.648
Short sentences with clear full stops sound natural, not rushed.

11
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:50.084
Keep one shared pronunciation list, so every deck your team makes sounds consistent.

12
00:00:50.584 --> 00:00:54.075
Once your notes sound right, turn the deck into video.

13
00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:58.684
On Pro, a.i. directs it, landing each term as the voice says it.

14
00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.217
Start at powerpoint2vid.com.

